  ==> A MECHANISM CLOSES THE SAG. What closes it, and how:
      - the PRESCRIBED AD form (Vc^2 = Vobs^2 + sigz^2 dln sigz^2/dln r) NEVER closes:
        task family spans -0.4360 .. -0.1794 across flares (it DEEPENS the sag).
      - the TEXTBOOK full-AD form closes it for flare >~ 0.09 (sigma_z >~ 10 km/s):
        full@flare=0.1 -0.0466, full@flare=0.2 +0.0412; at flare=0.04 (sigma_z ~ 5-7 km/s) residual -0.0995.
      - error-model stack alone (V6 err): -0.1250 [-0.1396,-0.1057] -> only ~12% closure; the sag is NOT an error artifact.
      - physical stack (err+fullAD): -0.0310 [-0.0496,-0.0102] (canon), -0.0373 (alt) -> V6 PASS.
      CAVEAT (honest): the closure is degenerate with the HI sigma_z calibration. The registered
      sag is reproduced as the pressure-support (asymmetric-drift) deficit of the gas for
      sigma_z ~ 10-16 km/s; at sigma_z <~ 7 km/s a residual sag of -0.10 dex/dex survives.

